  "limits": [
    "Native SDK values in SubCrv recipes measure whole source curves; local SDK-shaped values measure the temporary inputs. These scalar scopes are deliberately not compared. Status, printed command minima/maxima and emitted permanent marks are compared against actual native command history. Tests show changing whole-source SDK distances cannot affect those comparisons.",
    "All nine printed minima and eight printed maxima match within the observed display rounding plus 1e-6. The two-parts case retains the known asymmetric line-overlap failure: native maximum sqrt(8), local maximum 2. Interval-end mark sets match eight of nine; full permanent marks match four of nine. Tied witness locations remain different. No overlap or full command qualification is claimed.",
    "Reverse-open portions use reversed negated native domains; closed portions can cross the original seam into an extended domain. Source geometry remains unchanged in all final native and local recipes. Two portions of the same owner are locally tested, but native duplicate-owner getter behavior is not qualified by these distinct-owner recipes.",
    "The initial and discovery captures are exploratory retained observations from intermediate probe revisions. Only the final nine-case capture is tied to the current native probe source. The first broad nine-case capture was superseded by the richer source-invariance captures; no failing scalar or marker comparison was removed.",
    "The seven-check ASAN run instruments the current C ABI bridge and driver, linking uninstrumented helper and vendor static archives. Leak detection was disabled. This is not full vendor-kernel sanitizer or leak qualification and includes no performance measurement.",
    "Native calls used the existing owned private headless launcher and public SDK/command surface. Wine, FEX, license settings and vendor sources were not changed.",
    "Historical digest values and nonhash metadata are preserved using immutable Git references when shared files changed. The pre-existing 69 unverifiable historical records remain untouched."
  ],
